  "key_observations_html": "<div style=\"border:1px solid #C7D8E8;border-radius:10px;padding:0.75rem 0.95rem;margin:0.1rem 0 0.55rem;background:#ffffff;box-shadow:0 1px 3px rgba(15,23,42,0.06);\"><ul style=\"margin:0.1rem 0 0 1.05rem;padding:0;color:#1F4C67;font-size:0.9rem;line-height:1.45;\"><li><strong>RWA printed metrics were roughly flat this week:</strong> Distributed Value near $15.90B (-1.4% 30D) keeps on-chain RWA exposure in a holding pattern\u2014tokenization momentum is still news- and pipeline-driven until distributed value breaks range. Related: <a href=\"https://www.coindesk.com/business/2026/08/31/sberbank-plans-to-add-ether-and-usdt-as-collateral-for-crypto-backed-loans\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sberbank plans to add ether and USDT as collateral for crypto-backed loans: Report</a> (CoinDesk).</li><li><strong>Tokenized U.S. Treasuries remain the institutional bridge into RWAs:</strong> adoption is strongest where products plug into cash management, collateral, and liquidity workflows.</li><li><strong>Tokenized T-bill supply is still expanding through new products:</strong> That usually shows up first as new issuer and product supply, then as higher distributed value and denser collateral-style use across networks and platforms. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/markets/2026-08-31-hyperliquid-eyes-us-entry-kraken-parent-payward-perpetual-futures-deal-bloomberg-413129\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Hyperliquid seeks US foothold through Kraken parent Payward in crypto perpetuals deal: Bloomberg</a> (The Block).</li><li><strong>Regulatory framing still decides product access:</strong> Clearer rules tend to unlock balance-sheet participation and collateral workflows even when aggregate on-chain totals reprice slowly. Related: <a href=\"https://www.theblock.co/news/business/2026-08-31-russias-largest-bank-forecasts-46-billion-in-first-year-crypto-exchange-trading-under-new-rules-report-413082\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Russia\u2019s largest bank forecasts $46 billion in first-year crypto exchange trading under new rules: report</a> (The Block).</li></ul><p class=\"takeaways__note\">Context only\u2014not investment advice. Bullets combine on-page data with recent industry headlines.</p></div><p class=\"review-note ko-disclaimer\">Key observations are AI generated and should be reviewed for accuracy.</p>",
